  "scope_id": "KNOT-COUPLING-20261031-001",
  "title": "Counting on the knot's spaces: easy only at the knot's law and the dimer law",
  "subject": "The complexity of counting 2-colourings of non-2-colourable cubic triple systems weighted by lam per monochromatic line",
  "conclusion": "Counting 2-colourings of the knot's spaces with weight lam per monochromatic line is polynomial exactly at lam in {0, 1, -1, -3, oo} and #P-hard at every other complex lam, by chains of atoms and interpolation from the hard Pfaffian systems, with torsion points on the curve of two atom ratios closing the complex case. Beyond the affine couplings only the knot's law (count 0) and the dimer law (a determinant) are easy.",
